Game Inspirations
Monument Valley: this game has a minimal yet mystical visual style which I would like to emulate in our game. Characters, objects, and buildings are all designed with minimal detail but enough that you understand clearly where you are, what you are, and what you're doing. The world of this game is strange and intriguing which is communicated well through its unique character designs, architecture, and perspective.
Battle for Polytopia: this mobile game has plenty of stylised and bright visuals. Its use of vibrant colours and consistent palette makes for an upbeat and playful aesthetic. Similarily to Monument Valley, your perspective is orthographic which is a key angle depicted in our game so nailing visuals to work from this perspective is crucial. It makes use of its voxel asethetic well, allowing for some fun and interesting designs.